    {
      "hash": "da7e6ea7a5522a24f781cbbec7de1b65667ce8fc",
      "message": "odyssey: major io rework and refactoring\n\nThis patch moves Odyssey from stream based write caching\nto message driven. All write operations are delayed\nand happen on a group of messages.\n\nThis removes necessity to do IO and wait for write completion during calls\nfrom SSL_write() context. Write timings should behave more predictable now and\nnumber of used syscalls should be also decreased.\n\nThis patch also simplifies caching management. All clients are simply\nreusing cached messages without prolonged contention.\n\nSeveral configuration options are no longer used:\npipeline, cache, cache_chunk\n",
      "parent_commits": [
        "389b71bbdb564e8af6118dc151613aa37d2b80f8"
      ],
      "author": {
        "name": "Dmitry Simonenko",
        "email": "pmwkaa@gmail.com",
        "date": "2018-08-28T14:43:46Z"
      },
      "commiter": {
        "name": "Dmitry Simonenko",
        "email": "pmwkaa@gmail.com",
        "date": "2018-08-28T14:43:46Z"
      }
    },
